  "text": "Pet Oncology | Davies Veterinary Specialists\nPet Owners\n>\nMeet Our Team\nBeing referred to Davies\nFacilities\nThe Referral Process\nFact Sheets\nFAQ\nClient Care\nFinance and Insurance\nSustainability\nVet Professionals\n>\nAppointment Request Form\nEmergency Referrals\nRadiology Request Form\nTPLO Post Op Form\nBook CPD\nCPD Webinar Library\nPopular Downloads\nServices\n>\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency and Critical Care\nHearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nNursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy Services\nClient Care\nOur Team\n>\nAnaesthesia Team\nCardiology Team\nClient Care Team\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery Team\nDermatology Team\nEmergency & Critical Care Team\nDiagnostic Imaging Team\nGreen Group\nHearing Clinic Team\nFinance Team\nInternal Medicine Team\nInterns\nLeadership Team\nNeurology Team\nNursing Team\nOncology Team\nOphthalmology Team\nOrthopaedics Team\nPain Management Team\nPatient Care Assistants and Technicians\nTherapy Services Team\nSoft Tissue Surgery Team\nSupport Team\nJoin Our Team\nContact Us\nInsights\n>\nBlogs\nNews\nFact Sheets\nCase Studies\nNewsletters\nCPD\nEmergencies\n01582 883950\nRefer Here\nLog In / Register\nUPDATE: Please be aware that our opening hours have changed on Monday 19th September. Please contact us for any emergency care.\nPet Oncology\nPet oncology is a specialised branch of veterinary medicine that focuses on the diagnosis and treatment of cancer in animals. At Davies Veterinary Specialists\n,\nwe understand that cancer affects both cats and dogs, and we are committed to providing exceptional oncology care for your pets. Our team of experienced veterinarians and oncologists work together to create personalised treatment plans to ensure the best possible outcome for your animal.\nWhat is Pet Oncology?\nPet oncology is the field of veterinary medicine that deals with the diagnosis, treatment, and management of cancer in animals. It involves a comprehensive approach that includes advanced diagnostics, surgery, chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and palliative care. At Davies Veterinary Specialists we believe in delivering compassionate and cutting-edge oncology services to improve the quality of life for pets diagnosed with cancer.\nOncology for Cats\nCats can develop various types of cancer, including lymphoma, mammary tumours, and oral tumours. Our\ndedicated oncology team\nat Davies Veterinary Specialists has extensive experience in diagnosing and treating feline cancers. We understand the unique challenges associated with feline oncology and strive to provide the most effective and compassionate care for your cat.\nOncology for Dogs\nDogs, like humans, can be affected by different types of cancer, such as mast cell tumours, osteosarcoma, and hemangiosarcoma. Our skilled veterinary oncologists at Davies Veterinary Specialists are well-versed in canine oncology and are equipped to deliver personalised treatment plans tailored to your dog’s specific needs. We aim to offer the highest standard of care to enhance your dog’s quality of life and improve overall prognosis.\nCancer Treatment for Cats and Dogs\nAt Davies Veterinary Specialists we offer a range of advanced cancer treatments for both cats and dogs. Our comprehensive approach includes surgery, chemotherapy, targeted therapies, immunotherapy, and supportive car whilst partnering with other centres to provide radiation treatment where appropriate. Our experienced veterinary oncology team will work closely with you to develop a customised treatment plan that takes into account your pet’s overall health, specific cancer type, and individual needs.\nCancer Management for Pets\nCancer management is crucial for pets diagnosed with cancer. At Davies Veterinary Specialists we focus not only on treating the disease but also on providing palliative care and improving your pet’s quality of life. Our compassionate\nveterinary oncology team\nwill guide you through every step of the process, offering support, education, and resources to help you make informed decisions for your beloved pet. We are committed to ensuring that your pet receives the best possible care throughout their cancer recovery journey.\nLearn more about Davies Veterinary Specialists in our\npet owners\nsection.\nNeed to make a referral?\nGet in touch with us using the form below.\nRefer Now\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nPet Hearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nVeterinary Neurology and Neurosurgery\nVeterinary Nursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy and Fitness Services\nVeterinary Client Care\nAbout Us\nDavies Veterinary Specialists FAQs\nJoin Our Team\nSustainability\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\nManor Farm Business Park\n|\nHigham Gobion\n|\nHertfordshire\n|\nSG5 3HR\n|\nTel 01582 883950\nRegistered address: Friars Gate 1011 Stratford Road Solihull B90 4BN\n|\nRegistered in England & Wales 10790375\n|\nVAT Reg 195 092 877\nCookie Settings\n© 2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists,\nPart of Linnaeus, an Affiliate of Mars, Incorporated\nHosting and Maintenance by Clickingmad\nTerms of Service (New)\nTerms of Service (Old)\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookies Policy\nModern Slavery Act\nCustomer Charter\nComplaints\nGender Pay Gap Report\nAccessibility\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\n01582 883950\n©2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists",
